flowchart TB
    accTitle: The check of the release app
    accDescr: Before a bot asks for a token of the release app, it checks that the repository names the app in the variable RELEASE_AUTOMATION_CLIENT_ID and has its private key in the environment release. With both, it asks for the token and does its work. Without one, it says in an annotation and in its summary which one is missing and that the checklist sets it up. A bot whose work is what the app does, such as the blueprint bot, the settings bot or Renovate, then fails; one that only helps a pull request along, such as the fix bot or the branch bot, warns and goes on without the token.

    bot(["A bot that acts<br>as the release app"])
    check["`**Check that the release app is set up**<br>RELEASE_AUTOMATION_CLIENT_ID<br>and its private key`"]
    token["The token of the app,<br>then the work of the bot"]
    missing["`The annotation and the summary<br>name what is missing and<br>**blueprint.py checklist**`"]
    fails(["The blueprint, settings,<br>upstream bots, Renovate<br>and the Rollout fail"])
    warns(["The fix, branch, diagram,<br>screenshot, merge and release<br>bots warn and go on"])

    bot --> check
    check -->|both set| token
    check -->|one missing| missing
    missing --> fails
    missing --> warns

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class bot,check,missing bot
    class fails,warns person
    class token done
